    "created_at": "2016-02-10T23:52:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-10T23:52:36Z",
    "body": "The FF/IE behavior is basically required for keyboard navigation to work at all in some common cases.  The lack of this behavior in Chrome causes severe difficulties for some users (this was brought up as a problem during the TR restyle - they requested we add some scripting hacks to make it work), so it's not really a \"choice\".  At _minimum_ it should be explicitly recommended in the spec, so that browsers implementing focus navigation are reminded of it, but I'm personally of the opinion this is an a11y requirement and should be properly MUSTed.\n\nI haven't yet filed a Chrome bug.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
